@round2_organizational_endorsement
title: What about the endorsements of the non-partisan organizations?
subtitle: With [+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +] out of the running, it's a choice between [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +] and [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +].
on-arrival: {!
Q.organizational_endorsements_seen = 1;
if (Q.rlb_royalist) {
    Q.rlb_dufour = 0;
    Q.landed_other *= 0.9;
} else if (!Q.rlb_royalist) {
    Q.rlb_dufour = 1;
    Q.landed_other += 4;
    if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") {
        Q.landed_traditionalist += 2;
    } else {
        Q.landed_kvp += 2;
    }
}

Q.burgher_royalist += 2;
Q.burgher_other -= 2;
Q.guild_royalist += 4;
Q.guild_traditionalist -= 4;

!}
view-if: dufour_run and not gallax_support_dufour
max-visits: 1
go-to: round2_menu

Landed League - [? if rlb_dufour: <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span> ?][? if not rlb_dufour: <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span> ?]

Wardens - [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": Abstention?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span> ?]

Commonwealth National Association of Commercial Employees (Clerks' Guild) - <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span>

Pan-Commonwealth League (PCL) - <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>

United Patriotic Leagues (UPL) - <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>

Veterans' League - <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span>

Many <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> members defied orders by voting for [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +], while others remain firmly opposed to formal cooperation with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. The disappointing performance of [+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +] has led the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> to abandon its alliance with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and return to a stance of non-partisanship, blaming the party's lackluster support for their candidate for the poor showing.

The shift of many right-wing organizations toward [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]’s candidacy will cripple the parties caught between the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> and the extremes, polarizing the electorate between the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and the <span style="color: #9B0000;">Vaelists</span>—a strategy once championed by Mallin, now turned against him by his former ally.

[? if not rlb_dufour: The Landed League’s decision to endorse <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span> rather than abstain has triggered a sharp break with the organization’s moderate affiliates. Their Purl branch, the <span style="color: #006400;">**PFW**</span>, has been especially vocal, campaigning hard against the endorsement and in favor of [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]. Neither this backlash nor Mallin’s push for abstention has convinced the Landed League to reverse course, and millions of rural voters are now expected to turn out for [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] in the next election. ?]

